### Place an order. The row and its outbox record are committed together; nothing is published
### inline. Note the outboxId in the response - it turns up unchanged as the CloudEvents id.
POST http://localhost:5007/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "acme", "customerId": "cust-1", "total": 11.0 }

### Inspect the outbox record. Status goes Pending -> Delivered within a second or two.
GET http://localhost:5007/outbox/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Aggregate counters.
GET http://localhost:5007/outbox/stats

### What the subscriber received, on the other side of the broker.
GET http://localhost:5017/received

### Clear the subscriber's record of what it has seen.
DELETE http://localhost:5017/received

### What the sidecar fetched from the subscriber at startup.
GET http://localhost:5017/dapr/subscribe

### Publish straight to the sidecar, bypassing the outbox. Useful for proving the component works
### on its own - and for seeing what you give up: this publish is not transactional with anything.
POST http://localhost:3507/v1.0/publish/order-pubsub/order-events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "manual-1", "customerId": "cust-9", "total": 1.0 }
